# Report Screenshots

## Overview

This folder contains the original screenshots collected during the DAT515 CUPS Printer Discovery Exploitation and Attack Detection project.

The screenshots were captured across multiple laboratory sessions. Due to several system and Docker environment restarts, some screenshots were regenerated at different stages of the experiments. Therefore, this folder brings the relevant screenshots together to provide a complete visual record of the work.

## Contents

The screenshots provide supporting evidence for:

- Laboratory setup and Docker container configuration
- Network connectivity and CUPS port inspection
- Normal printer-discovery traffic and baseline captures
- Scapy-based attack execution and packet variations
- Victim-side CUPS logs and IPP communication
- Detection tool execution and security alerts
- CSV and JSON detection results
- CUPS configuration changes and mitigation testing
- Post-mitigation packet delivery and detector results

## Notes

- Screenshots may show different IP addresses because Docker networks and containers were recreated between laboratory sessions.
- Each screenshot should be interpreted according to the experiment and network configuration in which it was captured.
- The screenshots document the experiments performed and supplement the final report.
- The original PCAP files and detector output files are maintained separately in the repository.

**Course:** DAT515 – Cloud Computing  
**Institution:** University of Stavanger  
**Project:** CUPS Printer Discovery Exploitation and Attack Detection Using Scapy
